Experiment                    : starts at 2026-11-15 22:19:25.142960 (39038.210993)
Experiment                    : This experiment compares run time and resource consumption of Benchbase queries in different DBMS.
Benchbase data is generated and loaded using several threads. Loading uses a batch size of 128 rows per INSERT.
Benchmark is 'tpcc'. Scaling factor is 16. Target is based on multiples of '1024'. Factors for benchmarking are [16]. Benchmarking runs for 5 minutes.
TiDB uses 3 SUT replica(s) and 3 PD node(s).
Load durability is relaxed (-xld; restored after the load).
Experiment uses bexhoma version 0.11.18.
System metrics are monitored by a cluster-wide installation.
Experiment is limited to DBMS ['TiDB'].
Import is handled by 1 processes (pods).
Workers are fixed to cl-worker36, cl-worker37, cl-worker29.
Database uses ephemeral storage of size 50Gi.
Loading is tested with [1] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is tested with [16] threads, split into [1, 2] pods.
Benchmarking is run as [1] times the number of benchmarking pods.
Experiment is run once.
Maximum DBMS across the whole cluster is 10.
Results are validated against basic correctness requirements.
Distributed DBMS uses 3 worker nodes, 3 replicas and 0 shards per node.
SUT requests 4 CPU and 16Gi RAM.
